-- title:
--   Adelic spans embed equivariantly into copies of one irreducible representation
-- statement:
--   Fix real numbers $c,u,d_1,d_2$ with $d_1<d_2$, a finite set $T\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q})$, and put $D=\bigcup_{x\in T}\{g x : g\in \mathcal S\}$, where $\mathcal S=$ `centreCutSiegelSet ℚ c u d₁ d₂` consists of the $g$ whose finite part is integral, whose archimedean components have local height $\ge c$ and window square $\le u^2$ at every infinite place, and whose archimedean determinant norms lie in $[d_1,d_2]$; assume `CoversModCentre`, i.e. every $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q})$ can be written with $\gamma g z\in D$ for some $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q)$ and some central adelic scalar $z$. Let $\Theta_1,\Theta_2$ be Hecke eigensystems over $\mathbb Q$ with values in $\mathbb C$ (a nonzero level ideal together with families $a(v),b(v)$ indexed by the finite places) such that $a_1(v)=a_2(v)$ and $b_1(v)=b_2(v)$ for all $v$ outside a finite set. Let $R_1,R_2$ be smooth cuspidal realizations of $\Theta_1,\Theta_2$ at the production pins over $D$ formed from the level family $N\mapsto$ `levelOne` $(N)\sqcap$ `finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup`, the Hecke generators `heckeGen`, full centre, and the conditioning set `adelicBox` — each a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q})$, nonzero somewhere, with central character, smooth cuspidal automorphic, invariant under right translation by the level subgroup at its eigensystem's level, and a Hecke eigenfunction with eigenvalues $a(v)$ and central eigenvalues $b(v)$ away from a finite exceptional set — and assume both are genuine, i.e. continuous. Let $q$ be a prime. Then there are a type $V$ with a structure of complex vector space carrying an action of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$ commuting with the scalars such that `IsIrreducibleGLRep q V` holds ($V$ has a nonzero vector and every $\mathbb C$-submodule stable under $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$ is $\bot$ or $\top$), an index type $\iota$, and $\mathbb C$-linear maps $j_i:$ [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) $R_i.\mathrm{toFun}\to(\iota\to_0 V)$ for $i=1,2$, both injective and both commuting with the action of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$.
--
--   This is the formal counterpart of the passage from two cuspidal realizations with almost everywhere equal Hecke eigenvalues to a single local component at $q$: both spans sit inside a sum of copies of one irreducible admissible representation of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$, equivariantly and without collapsing. It feeds the irreducibility statement for the representation generated by a newform, [`CuspForm.IsNewform.isIrreducibleGLRep_of_linearMap_range_eq_span_padic_smul_self`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.isIrreducibleGLRep_of_linearMap_range_eq_span_padic_smul_self).
